00:00:25.699 --> 00:00:28.029
It is really not a good week for Donald Trump.

00:00:28.029 --> 00:00:35.121
The UK's Channel four has released a bombshell
investigation, exposing that in 2016, the

00:00:35.121 --> 00:00:41.480
Trump campaign actually had a specific strategy
to prevent black people from voting.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:48.420
Now, remember that publicly in 2016, Trump
was sort of paying lip service to how much

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:49.890
he loves black people.

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:54.290
Whereas my African-American, he said a couple
times during rallies saying he's gonna do

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:56.079
so well with black voters.

00:00:56.079 --> 00:01:01.109
But privately, they knew that black voters
were going to go overwhelmingly for Hillary

00:01:01.109 --> 00:01:02.109
Clinton.

00:01:02.109 --> 00:01:07.610
And rather than trying to convince black voters
to vote for Trump, what they did was to try

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:09.870
to keep black voters from voting altogether.

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:14.980
And the Channel four investigation really
well done exposes exactly how they did this.

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:17.150
And there's really a lot to go through here.

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:21.560
This was done through social media targeting
with very detailed analytics.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:27.390
The Trump campaign had three and a half million
black Americans in their database of about

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:33.770
200 million voters, and they categorized those
black Americans overwhelmingly under what

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:39.690
was called a deterrence campaign, meaning
deter folks from voting.

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:44.410
That's what the deterrence category was, people
that the campaign hopes do not vote.

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:52.840
So, for example, in Georgia, despite black
voters, Konsta black black Americans making

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:58.520
up 32 percent of the Georgia population, they
were 61 percent of the deterrence category

00:01:58.520 --> 00:01:59.780
in North Carolina.

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:04.700
Black people are 22 percent of the population,
but they were 46 percent of the deterrence

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:05.700
category.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:08.660
Similar numbers in Wisconsin and in other
places.

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:14.790
There were also Hispanic and Asian-Americans
disproportionately in these deterrence campaigns.

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:19.980
And meanwhile, the get out the vote campaigns
were disproportionately white voters.

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:25.530
And indeed, we can't say it was specifically
because of this, but certainly it played a

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:26.530
role.

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:31.680
Black turnout fell in 2016 for the first time
in 20 years.

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:39.760
The way they worked these campaigns included,
for example, using highly produced videos

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:42.269
containing clips of Hillary.

00:02:42.269 --> 00:02:48.420
Hillary Clinton using the term super predator
and showing those to the deterrence group

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:49.750
along with other tactics.

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:53.569
And again, the idea being dissuade black voters
from voting at all.

00:02:53.569 --> 00:02:56.909
They know that Trump's not going to do well
with the black voters.

00:02:56.909 --> 00:03:01.010
Try to get black voters to say, and I don't
know that I want to go out and vote for Hillary

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:02.870
and try to simply keep them home.

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:05.040
So there are a few things to discuss here.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:10.769
First of all, it's shocking to see it done
so brazenly, but it makes sense that the Trump

00:03:10.769 --> 00:03:13.950
campaign would try to deter black people from
voting.

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:16.700
Let's just be very, very real here.

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:22.430
The Trump campaign didn't make sense for black
voters or Latino voters or others because

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:25.430
their policies were not going to be good for
those groups, plain and simple.

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:30.450
So Hillary Clinton won the black vote 89 to
eight in 2016.

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:36.549
And Donald Trump's campaign identified that
if you if you can keep a group that is going

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:40.510
to skew so heavily in favor of Hillary Clinton
at home, it's good for you.

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:43.269
So it's not surprising from a mathematical
perspective.

00:03:43.269 --> 00:03:48.310
If you were Trump's campaign publicly, of
course, you say yes, black Americans vote

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:49.310
for Trump.

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:50.489
We're going to make it great for everybody.

00:03:50.489 --> 00:03:51.930
It's gonna be fantastic.

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:55.040
Privately, you know, they're not going to
vote for you and you're better off just trying

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:56.040
to keep them home.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:01.260
So it is a rational strategy given the numbers
and the data.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:06.640
Second, remember that the social media platforms
are a huge part of this.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:09.609
Facebook allowed this to be done.

00:04:09.609 --> 00:04:14.019
And indeed, Channel four, as part of their
investigation, went to Facebook and said,

00:04:14.019 --> 00:04:16.390
Farai, you know, do you have a comment on
this?

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:22.940
And Facebook said, listen, we've changed things
since 2016, which is a way of saying, yeah,

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:25.560
it happened in 2016 and we allowed it to happen.

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:31.840
They said we now have 35000 people working
to ensure the integrity of our platform.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:37.310
We now have rules that prohibit campaigns
that are trying to suppress the vote.

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:42.570
So they are conceding that this this happened
and that this took place.

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:47.470
So the platforms that allow this stuff are
a big part of the story.

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:52.660
In addition to a Republican platform that
is completely unappealing to black voters

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:53.660
and black.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:54.850
Voters accurately determine that.

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:58.860
But then there's a third part, which is Trump's
doing this again this year.

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:00.880
It's not being done in the exact same way.

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:07.300
But with voter purges in disproportionately
black areas, with fear campaigns, with intimidation

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:12.190
tactics, talking about, you know, Democrat
run urban areas and cities are going to have

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:16.040
police on Election Day and we're going to
be monitoring and blah, blah, blah.

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:20.280
The goal is the same, although the tactics
are different.

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:21.970
We can't let them win with it.

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:26.770
I predict very high turnout from black voters
this time around.

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:30.130
Whether that will lead to a Joe Biden electoral
victory.

00:05:30.130 --> 00:05:32.520
Well, we've got to go out and vote.

